uying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Liftoff Mobile, Inc. provides performance marketing and monetization solutions for the app economy. Its AI-powered platform, Cortex unifies marketing, creative, and monetization to deliver measurable performance across the app lifecycle. The company enables advertisers to unlock profitable user growth while helping app publishers maximize revenue with advanced ad monetization technology. It serves customer base across gaming, consumer, and emerging app categories. The company was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Redwood City, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeremy N. Bondy | CEO & Director | Age 37 | Compensation: $6.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 649 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $174K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 17% of revenue (significant) signals commitment to product development and talent.","financial_summary":["Liftoff Mobile, Inc. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $3.1B market cap on $686M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +9.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 84% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $113M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -9.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 56% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 48% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Large open-market insider purchases (net $60.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liftoff Mobile (NASDAQ:LFTO) Stock Jumps 8.1% \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/liftoff-mobile-nasdaqlfto-stock-jumps-8-1-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793917346.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liftoff Mobile (NASDAQ:LFTO) Nears Its Lows: Ready for Liftoff?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication/liftoff-mobile-nasdaqlfto-nears-its-lows-ready-for-liftoff","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793545680.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.414,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liftoff Mobile (NASDAQ:LFTO) Stock Gets Price Target Reduction from UBS Group","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/liftoff-mobile-nasdaqlfto-stock-gets-price-target-reduction-from-ubs-group.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793436787.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.572,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for October 28th (ABG, AWI, BRSP, CLS, CNC, COMP, FCX, LFTO, PROK, ST)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/28/analysts-price-target-changes-for-october-28th-abg-awi-brsp-cls-cnc-comp-fcx-lfto-prok-st.html","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793231068.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Is Liftoff Mobile (NASDAQ:LFTO) The Ad-Tech Comeback Story To Watch?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication/is-liftoff-mobile-nasdaqlfto-the-ad-tech-comeback-story-to-watch","date":"2026-10-19","timestamp":1792422480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liftoff Mobile, Inc. (NASDAQ:LFTO) Stock Has Consensus Price Target of $34.64 According to Analysts","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/10/liftoff-mobile-inc-nasdaqlfto-stock-has-consensus-price-target-of-34-64-according-to-analysts.html","date":"2026-10-10","timestamp":1791609307.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Liftoff Mobile combines AI growth prospects with discounted valuation, Wedbush says","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/liftoff-mobile-combines-ai-growth-165000752.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793119800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here are Tuesday's biggest analyst calls: SpaceX, Apple, Broadcom, CoreWeave, Palantir, Intel & more","source":"cnbc.com","link":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/27/biggest-calls-tuesday-on-wall-street-include-spacex-coreweave.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793103995.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liftoff to Announce Third Quarter 2026 Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/liftoff-announce-third-quarter-2026-200500568.html","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792699500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]}],"news_sentiment":{"score":0.371,"label":"Positive","bullish_pct":0.778,"bearish_pct":0.111,"article_count":9},"legal_filings":[{"form_type":"10-Q","filing_date":"2026-11-05","description":"10-Q","summary":"